<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ QueryREPA as MI maximization. ‣ 3.3 Contrastive Representation Alignment of Object Queries ‣ 3 Representation Alignment for Medical Object Detection ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> be the positive pair with joint <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> and marginals <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(u),p(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(u),p(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> i.i.d. negatives <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{V_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}\sim p(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{V_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}\sim p(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be sampled independently of <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define scores <math id="A1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(u,v)=\text{sim}(u,v)/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>sim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(u,v)=\text{sim}(u,v)/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(u,v)=\exp(s(u,v))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(u,v)=\exp(s(u,v))</annotation></semantics></math>. The InfoNCE objective of Eq. (<a href="#S3.E9" title="In QueryREPA as MI maximization. ‣ 3.3 Contrastive Representation Alignment of Object Queries ‣ 3 Representation Alignment for Medical Object Detection ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) can be expressed as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{QRA}}^{(l)}=-\mathbb{E}\left[\log{\frac{r(U^{(l)},V)}{r(U^{(l)},V)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}{r(U^{(l)},V_{k})}}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>QRA</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{L}}_{\text{QRA}}^{(l)}=-\mathbb{E}\left[\log{\frac{r(U^{(l)},V)}{r(U^{(l)},V)+\sum_{k=1}^{K}{r(U^{(l)},V_{k})}}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Introduce a uniformly random index <math id="A1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\in\{0,\cdots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\in\{0,\cdots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> and construct the candidate set <math id="A1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{V_{0},\cdots,V_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{V_{0},\cdots,V_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math> by placing the positive at slot <math id="A1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(V_{j}\sim p(v|U^{(l)}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(V_{j}\sim p(v|U^{(l)}))</annotation></semantics></math> and drawing the remaining <math id="A1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> elements i.i.d. from <math id="A1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(v)</annotation></semantics></math>. By Bayes’ rule and exchangeability,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(J=j\mid u,v_{0:K})=\frac{\frac{p(v_{j}\mid u)}{p(v_{j})}}{\sum_{m=0}^{K}\frac{p(v_{m}\mid u)}{p(v_{m})}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(J=j\mid u,v_{0:K})=\frac{\frac{p(v_{j}\mid u)}{p(v_{j})}}{\sum_{m=0}^{K}\frac{p(v_{m}\mid u)}{p(v_{m})}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">The model’s softmax over scores,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(J=j\mid u,v_{0:K})=\frac{r(u,v_{j})}{\sum_{m=0}^{K}r(u,v_{m})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(J=j\mid u,v_{0:K})=\frac{r(u,v_{j})}{\sum_{m=0}^{K}r(u,v_{m})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">is exactly the classifier used by InfoNCE.
The InfoNCE loss is the average cross-entropy between the true posterior <math id="A1.p2.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\cdot\mid u,v_{0:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot\mid u,v_{0:K})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p2.m16" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid u,v_{0:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid u,v_{0:K})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{QRA}}^{(l)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>QRA</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{QRA}}^{(l)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[-\log q_{\theta}\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[-\log q_{\theta}\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(p(\cdot\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K})\right)+\mathrm{KL}\!\left(p\|q_{\theta}\right)\right]\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo rspace="0.280em">]</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(p(\cdot\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K})\right)+\mathrm{KL}\!\left(p\|q_{\theta}\right)\right]\;\geq\;\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">Generate <math id="A1.p2.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z=(J,V_{0:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=(J,V_{0:K})</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> by adding i.i.d. negatives and randomly placing the positive. This defines a channel <math id="A1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z\mid v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z\mid v)</annotation></semantics></math> using only independent noise, so <math id="A1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U^{(l)}\to V\to Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U^{(l)}\to V\to Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a Markov chain. By the data processing inequality,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I\!\left(U^{(l)};V\right)\;\geq\;I\!\left(U^{(l)};Z\right)\;\geq\;I\!\left(U^{(l)};J\mid V_{0:K}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\!\left(U^{(l)};V\right)\;\geq\;I\!\left(U^{(l)};Z\right)\;\geq\;I\!\left(U^{(l)};J\mid V_{0:K}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> is uniform and independent of <math id="A1.p2.m22" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{0:K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{0:K}</annotation></semantics></math> under the random placement,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I\!\left(U^{(l)};J\mid V_{0:K}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I\!\left(U^{(l)};J\mid V_{0:K}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=H(J\mid V_{0:K})-H(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=H(J\mid V_{0:K})-H(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log(1+K)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>U</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log(1+K)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Combining Eq. (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and Eq. (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I\!\left(U^{(l)};V\right)\;\geq\;\log(1+K)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.742em;" width="0.742em"><mi>H</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\!\left(U^{(l)};V\right)\;\geq\;\log(1+K)-\mathbb{E}\!\left[H\!\left(J\mid U^{(l)},V_{0:K}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Eq. (<a href="#A1.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) to Eq. (<a href="#A1.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proofs ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\!\left(U^{(l)};V\right)\;\geq\;\log(1+K)-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{QRA}}^{(l)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.348em;" width="0.348em"><mi>I</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>QRA</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\!\left(U^{(l)};V\right)\;\geq\;\log(1+K)-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{QRA}}^{(l)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">which is the desired standard lower bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Ablation Study of Decoder Layer</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ablation study regarding the decoder layer <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> used for alignment in QueryREPA is given in Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Ablation Study of Decoder Layer ‣ Align Your Query: Representation Alignment for Multimodality Medical Object Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
The table shows that our method is capable of producing optimal results regardless of decoder layer <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.
In our main experiments, we choose layer index <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=5</annotation></semantics></math>, due to its slight increase (+0.1) in total AP.</p>
</div>
