<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A2.T4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of decoder layer index <math id="A2.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> for QueryREPA loss.</span> Results show that choosing <math id="A2.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=5</annotation></semantics></math> produces highest overall AP, but difference is minimal. Thus, our method is capable of producing optimal results robust to the choice of <math id="A2.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
